## If you have only **7 days** before the interview, focus on these in order:

1. Kotlin fundamentals and advanced features
2. Coroutines, Flow, StateFlow, and SharedFlow
3. Android SDK concepts (AAR, API design, initialization, versioning)
4. Gradle (`api` vs `implementation`), R8, and ProGuard
5. Performance and memory leak prevention
6. Networking and security (Retrofit, OkHttp, SSL pinning)
7. Mock interview questions and one hands-on SDK project (build a small library, package it as an AAR, and integrate it into a sample app)

This sequence covers the topics that are most frequently evaluated for Android SDK developer positions.
